# Paths `cargo tauri dev` must not restart the editor for.
#
# The dev watcher watches every workspace crate the editor depends on, and
# restarts the editor - killing whatever it was doing - when a file in one
# changes. Read from the common ancestor of those crates, which is this root.

# A web build regenerates the Lua runtime bundle when `lua-runtime.ts` is newer
# (`jengine_builder::web::lua_runtime_source`). It lives in `jengine-builder`,
# so a web build started from the editor restarted the editor halfway through.
# The build reads the bundle from disk, so the copy compiled into the running
# editor going stale changes nothing.
crates/jengine-builder/assets/lua-runtime.js

# Staged by build-editor-release.ps1 / .sh for a release; a dev editor never reads it.
editor/src-tauri/release-resources/
